layout "layout.faqir"

block content
  p
    | Click any station on the Floor (or any session link elsewhere) to open its page. It shows everything the session has
    | done, how much it cost, and the controls to steer it. The address is
    code {{ site.url }}/s/
    | followed by the session's id, so you can bookmark or share it.
  include "partials/shot.faqir" (assets=site.assets file="session-desktop.png" alt="A session page: the timeline on the left with a plan, a Bash command card and Claude's reply; the header card on the right with status, cost, tokens, context, duration and the control buttons." caption="A session on a computer: the timeline on the left, the header and side panels on the right.")
  p
    | On a computer the timeline fills the left side and the header with the side panels sits on the right. On a phone
    | the header comes first (tap
    strong More ▾
    | to see all of it) and the rest sits behind tabs:
    strong Timeline
    | ,
    strong Todos
    | ,
    strong Files
    | ,
    strong Git
    | ,
    strong Subagents
    | ,
    strong Progress
    | and
    strong Raw
    | .

  h2#header The header
  p From top to bottom, the header card shows:
  ul
    li
      strong The status
      | and badges:
      code paused
      | ,
      code walk mode
      | ,
      code job · running
      | (for sessions started as a job) and
      code stopping
      | (a stop was requested and has not taken effect yet).
    li
      strong The title
      | and a line with the project, the machine (links to Machines), the branch with its state (
      code ↑2
      | commits ahead,
      code ↓1
      | behind,
      code 3 dirty
      | files, or
      code clean
      | ) and the working folder.
    li
      strong A waiting banner
      | when the session needs you, for example "Waiting on you: Bash", with an
      strong Answer →
      | link to the Inbox.
    li
      strong Badges
      | for the model, the effort level, the permission mode and where it was started (
      code cli
      | ,
      code desktop
      | ,
      code headless
      | ), plus
      code imported
      | for sessions loaded with bb import.
    li
      strong Six numbers.
      strong Cost
      | (with lines added and removed),
      strong Tokens in / out
      | (with the cache hit rate),
      strong Context
      | (with the number of compactions),
      strong Duration
      | ,
      strong Waiting on me
      | (the total time Claude has spent waiting for you, including a wait in progress) and
      strong Last event
      | (with the reason once it has ended).

  h2#controls The controls
  p These buttons act on this one session. They disappear once the session has ended.
  dl
    dt
      strong Walk mode
    dd
      | Turns walk mode on or off for this session only. Once you have set it here it wins over the machine and global
      | settings, even if you later switch the global walk mode off. See
      a(href="/docs/walk-mode#which-wins") which setting wins
      | .
    dt
      strong Notify
    dd
      | On by default. Switch it off to mute every notification about this session (it still shows in the Inbox and the
      | attention bar).
    dt
      strong ❚❚ Pause
      | /
      strong ▶ Resume
    dd
      | Holds the session at its next tool call until you resume it. Claude can still finish the sentence it is writing;
      | it just cannot run anything. A pause lasts at most about 9½ minutes per tool call; after that the tool runs and
      | the next one is held again.
    dt
      strong ■ Stop
    dd
      | Asks "Stop this session?"; press
      strong Yes, stop
      | to confirm. Anything the session is waiting on is released (a pending permission is denied), and at its next tool
      | call Claude is refused and halted. If the session is a Buildyboy job, its process is also ended on the machine.
    dt
      strong Remote Control ↗
    dd Only shown when Claude Code's own Remote Control was active in this session.
    dt
      strong Export .md
    dd
      | Downloads the whole session as a Markdown file named
      code session-xxxxxxxx.md
      | .
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      p
        strong Stop and Pause act at the next tool call.
        | A session that is idle at its prompt, or only writing text, is not affected until it runs a tool. And a new
        | prompt typed at the terminal cancels a pending stop.
  p Below the buttons, three rows with a Copy button each give you ready-made commands:
  ul
    li
      code claude --resume <id>
      | to continue this session in a terminal,
    li
      code claude --desktop --resume <id>
      | to continue it in the Claude desktop app,
    li
      code cd <folder>
      | to go to its working folder first.

  h2#timeline The timeline
  p
    | The timeline is the session's story, newest at the bottom. It follows new activity live while you are scrolled to
    | the bottom; scroll up and it stops following and offers
    strong ↓ Jump to live
    | with a count of new items. Near the top,
    strong Load older
    | fetches earlier history.
  p What you will see in it:
  ul
    li
      strong Your prompts
      | , right-aligned and labelled
      code YOU
      | (a subagent's instructions are labelled
      code TASK PROMPT
      | ).
    li
      strong Claude's replies
      | under
      code CLAUDE
      | , formatted as Markdown. Links open in a new tab; HTML is shown as text, never run.
    li
      strong Thinking
      | , folded away by default.
    li
      strong Tool cards
      | , one per tool call (below). In compact mode each is a single line until you open it.
    li
      strong Event rows
      | with a coloured dot: grey for information, amber for warnings, red for errors. Tap one to see its details. Two
      | kinds are worth knowing:
      code Decision
      | rows record how a request was answered ("Allowed Bash by web after 12s"), and
      code Watcher
      | rows record Buildyboy's own warnings (stale, loop suspected, budget, context).
    li
      strong Unrecognised transcript lines
      | , a single
      code raw
      | line naming the line's type, for kinds of transcript line Buildyboy does not know yet. Tap it to see the JSON.
  h3#compact Compact and detailed
  p
    | Next to the lane chips,
    strong Compact
    | and
    strong Detailed
    | switch how tool calls are shown. Compact is the default: prompts and Claude's replies are shown in full, and each
    | tool call is one line with its tool, a short summary (the command's description, the file with
    code +added −removed
    | , the pattern and match count, the page address) and how long it took. Tap a line to open its full card; tap the
    | card's top row to fold it again. Three or more tool calls in a row with nothing between them fold into one line
    | such as
    code 8 tools · Bash ×5, Read ×2, Edit ×1
    | (flagged when one of them was interrupted or exited non-zero). Failed, denied and blocked calls, questions and
    | plans always stay as full cards.
    strong Detailed
    | shows every card open, as below. Your choice is remembered in this browser.
  h3#tool-cards Tool cards
  p
    | Every card shows the tool's name, a
    code failed
    | ,
    code denied
    | ,
    code interrupted
    | or pulsing
    code running
    | label when relevant, how long it took and when. Failed and denied cards have a red border. Each kind of tool gets
    | its own layout:
  ul
    li
      strong Bash
      | : the command, an
      code exit 0
      | badge (green) or a red one for failures, and the output, opened automatically when the command failed or is short.
    li
      strong Edit, Write, MultiEdit
      | : the file and a coloured diff with
      code +added −removed
      | counts.
    li
      strong Read, Grep, Glob
      | : the file or pattern and how much was read or matched, with the matches folded away.
    li
      strong WebSearch and WebFetch
      | : the query or address, the HTTP status, and the results.
    li
      strong Agent (subagents)
      | : the task, the subagent's type, its result, and a button to open its lane.
    li
      strong TodoWrite
      | : the checklist, with ☑ done, ◐ in progress and ☐ pending items.
    li
      strong AskUserQuestion and ExitPlanMode
      | : the questions with the chosen answers, or the plan.
  h3#lanes Lanes and subagents
  p
    | Above the timeline,
    strong Main
    | shows the main conversation. When Claude starts subagents, each gets a chip such as
    code ✣ general-purpose · 4
    | that shows only that subagent's work, and
    strong All
    | shows everything interleaved.

  h2#side-panels The side panels
  dl
    dt
      strong Todos
    dd Claude's current to-do list, with how many items are done.
    dt
      strong Files
    dd Every file the session changed, with a bar showing how often, and the added and removed lines. Tap a file to see each change as a diff.
    dt
      strong Git
    dd
      | Pull requests (with review and check status, if you added a GitHub token in
      a(href="/docs/settings#github") Settings
      | ), commits made during the session, and snapshots of the branch state.
    dt
      strong Subagents
    dd Each subagent with its type, status, duration and a link to its lane.
    dt
      strong Progress
    dd
      | The latest
      code PROGRESS.md
      | the session wrote. Harness runs keep this file up to date; the "Next" and "Decisions" sections are highlighted.
      | It is captured at the end of each turn, when it changed.
    dt
      strong Raw
    dd The last 500 raw hook events, for when you want to see exactly what was recorded.

  h2#compose Sending a message
  p
    | The box at the bottom lets you talk to a running session from anywhere. Type in
    strong Message Claude…
    | and press
    strong Send
    | (or
    kbd Ctrl
    | +
    kbd Enter
    | ;
    kbd Cmd
    | +
    kbd Enter
    | on a Mac). The quick buttons
    strong continue
    | ,
    strong run the tests
    | ,
    strong commit and push
    | and
    strong stop here
    | send their text immediately, with no confirmation.
  p The switch on the left chooses when the message is delivered:
  ul
    li
      strong After turn
      | (the default): when Claude finishes its current turn, your message becomes its next instruction and it carries on.
    li
      strong Now
      | : Claude sees the message at its next tool call, as an extra note ("Message from the user (sent via Buildyboy)"),
      | without waiting for the turn to end.
  p
    | Queued messages show above the box with a
    strong Cancel
    | button until they are delivered;
    code ▸ N delivered
    | lists the last few that were.
  +callout(variant="warning")
    @content
      p
        strong A message does not wake up an idle session.
        | If the session is sitting at its prompt, an "After turn" message waits for the end of the next turn and a "Now"
        | message for the next tool call. The exception is a session holding at the end of a turn in walk mode: then your
        | message answers it straight away. Also,
        strong stop here
        | is just a message to Claude; to actually stop, use
        strong ■ Stop
        | .
  p
    | Once a session has ended the box is replaced by a note: resume it with
    code claude --resume
    | to continue.

  h2#replay Replay
  p
    | Press
    strong ⟲ Replay
    | to watch the session again. A bar appears with a play button, a time counter and a slider; on a computer a station
    | card re-enacts the lamp, the activity line and the belt. Play advances one event at a time; drag the slider to jump.
    | Replay covers the items already loaded in the current lane.
    strong Exit replay
    | returns to the live view.
